<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Wenxuan of Northern Qi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">526–559</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> · Also known as Gao Yang</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emperor Wenxuan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-qi">Northern Qi</a>, born <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gao">Gao</a> Yang, was a son of the general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gao-huan">Gao Huan</a>, who had dominated the Eastern Wei. In 550 he forced Emperor Xiaojing to abdicate and founded the Northern Qi dynasty with its capital at Ye. His early reign was energetic, but his later years were notorious for drunkenness and cruelty.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emperor-wenxuan-of-northern-qi.jpg" alt="Emperor Wenxuan of Northern Qi" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 张居正 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%B8%9D%E9%89%B4%E5%9B%BE%E8%AF%B4_%E9%AB%98%E6%B8%85_(page_131_%E9%AB%98%E6%B4%8B).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
